9131.synopsis:
Waits for a key on the hall of fame page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP
goes to the first application's help (cr_hlp), RIGHT to MTH_Copyright, ENTER to cr_waitkey;
MENU, UP, DOWN and LEFT wait again.

15127.synopsis:
Key table of the alarm list for KeyJump0: entries of a key code byte and a handler word,
ended by 0. Codes $01 to $06 run AlmSet, AlmClear, AlmView, AlmExit, AlmLoad and AlmSave;
right, left, up, down and ENTER run Alm_Right, Alm_Left, Alm_Up, Alm_Down and Alm_Enter.

4481.synopsis:
Diary's MTH commands: the command block that DiaryDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH
code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:
Blocks (10 commands), Cursor (23), Edit (14, 2 hidden) and Files (2). Layout: CMD_MARK (0);
one mthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name,
help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again);
TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK.

10344.synopsis:
Reads the source file name into f_SourceName at column 21, row 1 of the current window;
falls into InputLine.
Entry: f_SourceName = the text to edit Exit, Error: as InputLine.

2848.synopsis:
Help text of the card selection window: centre justification, no scrolling or cursor, then
"Select card with 0 - 3 (bold) or move cursor over card, ENTER to select" on separate lines;
null-terminated.
